# 25. `/actuator/info`

The info endpoint provides application/build information.

```text
GET /actuator/info
```

We can configure our own application information.

Example:

```yaml
info:
  app:
    name: Banking Application
    description: Banking management system
    version: 1.0.0
```

Then:

```text
GET /actuator/info
```

can return:

```json
{
  "app": {
    "name": "Banking Application",
    "description": "Banking management system",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  }
}
```

---

# 26. `spring.application.name`

We can also define:

```yaml
spring:
  application:
    name: banking-application
```

This gives the Spring application a name.

It is different from:

```yaml
info:
  app:
    name: Banking Application
```

The first identifies the application within the Spring ecosystem; the second is information we choose to expose through `/actuator/info`.

---

# 27. Build Information

Spring Boot can expose Maven build information.

The Maven plugin can be configured with:

```xml
<plugin>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
    <executions>
        <execution>
            <goals>
                <goal>build-info</goal>
            </goals>
        </execution>
    </executions>
</plugin>
```

After:

```text
mvn clean package
```

build information can be available through:

```text
/actuator/info
```

For example:

```json
{
  "build": {
    "artifact": "cruds",
    "name": "cruds",
    "version": "0.0.1-SNAPSHOT",
    "group": "com.example"
  }
}
```

---

# 28. Git Information

Actuator can also expose Git-related information such as:

```text
branch
commit ID
commit time
```

This can help identify exactly which source-code version is deployed.

For example:

```text
Production
    |
    v
/actuator/info
    |
    v
Commit: abc123
```

This is useful when troubleshooting deployed applications.

---

# 29. Security Considerations

Actuator endpoints can expose internal application information.

Examples include:

```text
/actuator/beans
/actuator/mappings
/actuator/loggers
```

Therefore, don't expose every Actuator endpoint publicly.

Avoid blindly using:

```yaml
management:
  endpoints:
    web:
      exposure:
        include: "*"
```

in a production banking application.

Prefer exposing only what is required:

```yaml
management:
  endpoints:
    web:
      exposure:
        include:
          - health
          - info
          - metrics
```

Later, Spring Security can be used to protect sensitive management endpoints.

